---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/consts';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | Patrik Alexits" description="How pa-tech.dev handles your data.">
	<main class="page-container">
		<section class="privacy-policy">
			<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
			<p>Last updated: 14 October 2026</p>

			<h2>Who is responsible</h2>
			<p>{SITE.name} is responsible for this website and the data processing described here. This is a personal site; I offer no goods or services through it. You can reach me at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>

			<h2>Visiting the site</h2>
			<p>To deliver the pages, the host processes your IP address. It does not store it after the request. I see no IP addresses and no visit logs.</p>
			<p>This site sets no cookies. It has no analytics, tracking, forms or third-party content. Your light or dark theme choice is stored in your browser's localStorage and never leaves your device.</p>

			<h2>Writing to me</h2>
			<p>If you email me, I process your address and your message to reply. I delete them when the conversation is over, unless the law requires me to keep them.</p>

			<h2>Recipients</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>statichost.eu, Sweden, hosts the site under a data processing agreement. It uses Hetzner Online GmbH, Germany, and BunnyWay d.o.o., Slovenia.</li>
				<li>Proton AG, Switzerland, handles my email.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>Your data stays in Switzerland and the EEA. I share it with no one else.</p>

			<h2>Legal basis</h2>
			<p>I process this data out of a legitimate interest in delivering a working, secure website and in answering your messages (Swiss revDSG Art. 31(1); where the GDPR applies, Art. 6(1)(f)).</p>

			<h2>Your rights</h2>
			<p>You can ask me what data I hold about you and ask me to correct or delete it, or object to its processing. Write to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. You can also complain to the Swiss <a href="https://www.edoeb.admin.ch/en">Federal Data Protection and Information Commissioner (FDPIC)</a> or, in the EU or EEA, to the data protection authority where you live.</p>

			<h2>Links to other sites</h2>
			<p>This site links to other websites. Their own privacy policies apply there.</p>

			<h2>Changes</h2>
			<p>When the site changes how it handles data, I update this page and its date.</p>
		</section>
	</main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.page-container { padding: var(--space-8); max-width: var(--size-prose); margin: 0 auto; }
	.privacy-policy h1 {
		color: var(--font-color-bold);
		margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
		letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-tight);
		font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
		font-size: var(--font-size-2xl);
		line-height: var(--line-height-xl);
	}
	.privacy-policy h2 {
		color: var(--font-color-bold);
		margin: var(--space-10) 0 var(--space-2);
		font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
		font-size: var(--font-size-xl);
		line-height: var(--line-height-lg);
	}
	.privacy-policy p + p { margin-block-start: var(--space-4); }
	.privacy-policy ul { margin-block: 0 var(--space-4); padding-inline-start: var(--space-6); }
</style>
